{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Hypnotic Eye feels like a natural next listen because my recent interest in Benmont Tench gives me a specific connection to Tom Petty and the Heartbreakers.",
    "Standing in the Breach appeals to my interest in thoughtful songwriting, while the blues and roots leanings of several other choices fit what drew me to Memphis and Old Sock."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Sonic Highways offers a harder-driving sound than I want right now; sharing a broad rock identity with my recent listening does not make it equally appealing.",
    "The folk emphasis of Sigh No More and the bright pop direction of A Head Full of Dreams are less compelling to me in this session than blues, roots music, and reflective songwriting."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to treat interest in established rock musicians as interest in a much wider range of rock sounds than I would actually choose now.",
    "Mellow or atmospheric music seems to be treated as an automatic match, but Morning Phase and The Endless River are only tentative interests when I am looking for songs and songwriting that connect more directly."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The specific musical connection between Benmont Tench and the Heartbreakers matters more to my immediate choice than a general resemblance between rock albums.",
    "I rarely choose something unless the connection feels strong: being curious enough to sample Springsteen or Alabama Shakes is different from wanting to commit to Hypnotic Eye or Standing in the Breach."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The choices recognize my interest in roots-oriented rock and established songwriters, but stretch that interest too broadly across sounds I am less inclined to choose right now."
}"}
